According to a report by IntelMarketResearch, the global Standardized Texture Modified Foods Market was valued at USD 419 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 639 million by 2034, expanding at a CAGR of 6.3% during the forecast period. Standardized texture modified foods, also known as care or therapeutic foods, are specially formulated meals designed for individuals whose medical conditions limit their ability to consume regular food textures. These products can be prepared in pureed, minced, soft or other standardized consistencies and may be fortified with protein, fiber, vitamins and minerals.
